In yet another of my many failed attempts to survive to the altar
in Mines and trade nasty yellow lucre for a chance at a better
life, I managed to make it to Mines Six as an AC 2 knight with
over 1600 zorkmids due to the high turn-around in a liquor shop
when a well-bribed pony is doing the shopping:

You followed a strict vegan diet.
You never hit with a wielded weapon.
You were a pacifist.
You never genocided any monsters.
You never polymorphed an object.
You never changed form.
You used no wishes.

But even so,

1) I shouldn't have assumed a hobbit was peaceful just because the
   last one had been, and
2) I really, really, really need to learn to watch my hitpoints;
   walking any other direction but diagonally by the hobbit would
   have been an improvement, and
3) I need to learn to Let .. The Pet .. Go First.  Whinney had
   already earned a promotion to "horse".

Sigh.  They call it the protection "racket", but I'm starting to
think more "sham" in my case.

Time to roll up another random character.  I save a lot of rent on
individual adventurers by not using any one of them for too long, and
I _do_ get a volume discount from the RNG, but my savings are getting
lost on the sad telegrams and memorial flowers overhead of going
through so many of them so fast: four today already and it's not 3AM
local time yet.

